This project uses this GitHub repo:

git@github.com:mondyv/Wheres-The-Brainrot.git

The main branch is:

master

Before starting any coding/editing task, always run:

git status
git pull origin master

After finishing any changes, always run:

git status
git add .
git -c user.name="limeladzs" -c user.email="limeladzs@gmail.com" commit -m "short clear description of what changed"
git pull --rebase origin master
git push origin master

Never skip the pull or push step.

Never use force push.

If there are no changes to commit, do not make an empty commit. Say there were no changes.

If git pull or git pull --rebase creates merge conflicts, stop and explain which files conflict before editing them. Do not randomly overwrite files.

If push is rejected because the remote branch changed, run git pull --rebase origin master, resolve safely if needed, then push again.
